# Findings that are known false positives, ignored by exact fingerprint.
#
# Prefer this over an [allowlist] regex in .gitleaks.toml: an allowlist entry
# widens the ruleset for every future scan, while a fingerprint retires one
# already-published finding. Note that gitleaks' allowlist regexes are matched
# against the *secret* by default (regexTarget = "secret"), not the line, so an
# entry shaped like the surrounding code will silently match nothing.
#
# Fingerprints embed the commit SHA, so these stop applying if the commits below
# are rebased or squashed away. That is the intended failure mode: re-decide
# rather than carry a stale suppression forward.

